# Uploads, locked files, and e-sign

## Uploads

- There is no Letters tab. Collection letters live on **Uploads**, grouped by
  type (`collection_letter` or `is_collection_letter`).
- `?tab=letters` must keep redirecting to Uploads.

## Delete lock

- **Locked for everyone:** Collection Letter and POA (`poa_document`, `poa`,
  `poa_signed`, `power_of_attorney`).
- **Not locked:** CC Authorization (manual uploads). Signed e-sign files stay
  undeletable via `esign_requests`, including signed CC Auth.
- Enforce in the UI, `deleteOwnClientDocument` / `deleteClientDocument`, and RLS
  (`lock_permanent_client_document_deletes`). Check e-sign protection with the
  **service role**, not staff RLS.

## E-Sign

- The engine is CRM-native: tokenised `/sign/[token]` + OTP + SHA-256 +
  certificate of completion, with `pdf-lib` stamping and `pdfjs-dist` page
  rasterising. There is no third-party e-sign provider.
- Field placement is data-driven: percent-based boxes with a `bind` key from
  `ESIGN_BIND_KEYS`, placed by drag-and-drop in `EsignDocumentBoard` (mode
  `edit`) and saved as JSON. Never go back to absolute-point field maps.
- `pdfjs-dist` is pinned to `3.11.174` with `canvas: false` aliased in
  `next.config.mjs`. Do not bump it opportunistically.
- Client `/sign/[token]` and `/api/sign/*` stay public (tokenised). Middleware
  must allow those paths **before** auth redirects.
- Client sign links use `publicAppUrl()` (`lib/constants/business-contact.ts`).
  Never hardcode an origin.
- Kill switch: `ESIGN_ENABLED=false`. Unset = **on**.
- Keep `send-invite-email.ts` spam-resistant: plain text + HTML, `reply_to`
  support, brand in the subject, no emojis or all-caps CTAs, visible site and
  full link.
- The signed Welcome Packet is stored as `poa_signed`, which both satisfies the
  Account Manager stage gate and drives POA auto-advance. CC Auth must **not**
  auto-stage. See `.cursor/rules/onboarding-stage-gates.mdc`.
- Required review fields (`lib/esign/review-fields.ts`): CC Auth — Name,
  Account Manager, MID, Card 1 last 4, Card 1 amount. Amount authorized stays
  optional (it totals from the card amounts). Welcome Packet — MID only.
  Cards 2–5 stay optional. Empty required fields highlight when Confirm Before
  Sending opens. Client name stamps in Title Case. Account Manager is **first
  name only**, Title Case.

### Planned: MID-scoped templates

Documents are being moved from the hardcoded `EsignKind` union to rows in
`esign_templates`, owned by a MID. The hard requirement is that adding a MID and
its documents stays **fully no-code**: an admin enters a MID name, uploads PDFs,
and places fields in the existing editor. When that lands, delete the `EsignKind`
union, `defaultLayoutForKind`, the bundled PDFs under `lib/esign/templates/` and
`public/esign-templates/`, and the matching `next.config.mjs` /`vercel.json`
bundling entries. Do not add a new hardcoded kind in the meantime.

## Attorney portal

- Do not drop `/api/clients/documents/download` from
  `ATTORNEY_PORTAL_API_ALLOWLIST`.
